#*************************************************************************
#                          Reweight Module                               *
#            Matrix-element and PDF reweighting for MG7 outputs          *
#*************************************************************************
#
# Two programs can reweight the events of an MG7 output, and both read this
# card:
#  - MadtRex (madtrex/, 'install madtrex' in MadGraph): matrix-element and
#    PDF/scale reweighting on the events as written (lhe or lhe_npy)
#  - the classic reweighting module (Mattelaer, arXiv:1607.00763): needs
#    f2py; LO and NLO reweighting, density matrices and plugins
# By default (change backend auto) MadtRex reweights whenever it can run the
# card, else the classic module. The launch question's reweight switch
# (classic/madtrex) or 'generate_events --reweight-backend=...' choose
# explicitly, and win over the line below.
#
# Note:
#   1) the value of alpha_s will be used from the event so the value in
#      the param_card is not taken into account.
#   2) It is (in general) dangerous/wrong to change parameters by a large
#      amount, if this changes the shape of the matrix elements a lot.
#      (For example, changing a particle's mass by much more than its
#      width leads to very inaccurate result). In such a case, separate
#      event generation runs are needed.
#
#************************************************************************
# ENTER YOUR COMMANDS BELOW.
#************************************************************************

#change backend auto   # classic | madtrex | auto

#change helicity True  # reweight each event at its own helicity (default),
                       # False: helicity-summed matrix elements

launch

#  SPECIFY THE PARAMETERS TO CHANGE LIKE THIS:
# set sminputs 1 130 # modify 1/alpha_EW
# set MT 175         # a parameter by its param_card name


#************************************************************************
# Example of code for the computation of two weights:
#
# launch --rwgt_name=mt175  ! start the computation of the first weight
#  set BLOCKNAME ID VALUE   ! rule to modify the current param_card
#  set MT 175               ! or by the parameter's param_card name
# launch                    ! start to compute a second weight
#  set MT scan:[170, 180]   ! one weight per value
#
# Note: The commands to specify the parameters are AFTER the associated
#       "launch".
#
#************************************************************************
# Options ('change NAME VALUE', before the first 'launch'), both programs:
#
# change backend classic|madtrex|auto : who reweights (default auto)
# change helicity True|False : helicity reweighting (default True). MadtRex
#        stops on events without helicity information when True.
# change mode LO : parameter (matrix-element) reweighting, the default
# change model NAME / change process DEF : reweight with another model
#        (MadtRex needs both lines). The weights are the new model's matrix
#        element over the original one the events were generated with;
#        MadtRex requires the regenerated subprocesses to match the original
#        ones (same particles, flavours and helicities).
#
# MadtRex only:
# change mode pdf : the lines that follow are PDF/scale reweighting:
#        launch --rwgt_name=nnpdf
#         set PDF_SET NNPDF40_nnlo_as_01180  ! or BEAM1_PDF_SET + BEAM2_PDF_SET
#         set MUF_FACTOR 2                   ! or MUR_FACTOR, MUF, MUR (GeV)
#        'change mode LO' switches back to parameter reweighting.
# change fptype d|f|m : floating-point precision to reweight to (also per
#        launch)
# change verbose|max_batch|max_deferred_iterations|streaming|
#        stream_batch_size VALUE : MadtRex driver tuning
# change alpha_s_power|scale_variation_output VALUE : PDF reweighting options
#
# Classic module only:
# change mode NLO|NLO_tree|LO+NLO : NLO reweighting (NLO samples)
# change output default|2.0|unweight, change rwgt_dir PATH,
# change tree_path/virtual_path PATH, change systematics, change multicore,
# change boost, change process DEF --add, a param_card given by its path,
# density-matrix options (change particle_in_density_matrix ...) and
# reweighting plugins.
#
# Manual: https://cp3.irmp.ucl.ac.be/projects/madgraph/wiki/Reweight
#         madtrex/README.md
#************************************************************************
